// Ch10 B09 "The farewell-tide" (C → E, 3 min) and B10 "Outside the causeway" (C, 1.5 min).
// act2_ch10.md §2 B09–B10. THE CHAPTER WHERE THE MOTES GO UP (rule 1): every mote in Reedhollow rises in
// a slow vertical spiral and turns glimmer_lift gold as it climbs; nothing drifts sideways or down, and
// no mote goes toward the singers, the party or Kerrid.
// T01: the clutch (twenty to thirty) at the waterline in a long shallow arc, facing the lagoon; the party
// back on the shore, Asha in front. No Order hum: the Kirru sing. T02 (held input, "Hold to watch"): the
// song begins, wordless and rising (`farewell_tide`, which carries the Letting's first cell). T03: THE
// CLOUD BREAKS straight overhead; the first stars; F02 is the hero frame. T04: at the top note the clutch
// TURNS ITS BACK to the water, all at once; on the release the song ends and the motes are gone.
// The prompt changes to "Release" at the peak, and the player ends the rite by letting go (act2_ch10.md §9 UI 1):
// M4-CIN-1304 stages it with the release gate (release_input, M4-CIN-1302). The clutch turns at the top note; the
// rite holds there for as long as the player holds, and the song ends on the release.
// T05: Asha has NOT turned around; Ysolde turns her by the shoulder (her warmth as an instruction).
// Rhen is already turned (he copies the room); Toma turns last, slowly.
title: ch10_farewell_tide
location: ch10/reedhollow
---
@letterbox on
@camera T01
@music silence fade=2.0
@mark asha shore_front walk
@wait 3.0
@camera T02
@music farewell_tide fade=0.5
<<event hold_input hold_to_watch>>
@vfx glimmer_lift at=lagoon_motes count=24 motion=spiral_up rate=slow
@wait 6.0
@camera T03 blend=3.0 ease=in_out_sine
@vfx glimmer_lift at=lagoon_motes count=48 motion=spiral_up rate=slow
@wait 6.0
@camera F02
@wait 6.0
<<event hold_input_end>>
@camera T04
@anim clutch turn_back
<<event release_input release_tide>>
@wait 1.5
@camera T05
@wait 2.0
Ysolde [tender]: Turn around. They asked us not to stay watching. #line:ch10_tide_001
@anim asha turn_back
@anim rhen turn_back
@wait 1.0
@anim toma turn_back
@wait 2.0
@camera T06
@wait 1.5
<<if $ch09_ebbing_danced>>
    Asha [grief]: Mine went down. #line:ch10_tide_002 #tn:"Her Ebbing at Corrow led the dead down into the sea; these went up."
<<endif>>
<<set $ch10_tide_witnessed = true>>
<<jump ch10_outside_causeway>>
===
// B10 "Outside the causeway" (C, 1.5 min, no dialogue). R07: outside the gate, PELL stands with his back
// to the water and to the whole rite, turned away as the clutch turned, for three strangers. KERRID stands
// beside him facing the other way, toward the water, watching the gold go up. Back to back, one held and
// one scraped. R08: an insert of Kerrid's forearm, the faintest held cyan in the scar (ADR 0022 (g); the
// first time). ≤ 2 s, no mote leaves him or comes to him, nobody sees it, nothing in the score marks it.
title: ch10_outside_causeway
---
@camera R07
@wait 4.0
@camera R08
@vfx glimmer_held at=kerrid_scar count=1 rate=slow
@wait 1.8
@camera R07
@wait 2.5
@music silence fade=3.0
@fade out 2.0
@letterbox off
===
